tps://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/15864/geno-smith"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/15864/geno-smith"}}}}},{"id":184497,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:20~l:28~a:3912547","guid":"938f19a1-ef9b-618c-2365-d55291e0fcc6","description":"Sam Darnold","sportId":28,"athleteId":3912547,"athlete":{"id":3912547,"description":"Sam Darnold","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3912547/sam-darnold"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3912547/sam-darnold"}}}}},{"id":444378,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:20~l:28~a:4430807","guid":"6667bcb0-dad1-3345-8e5a-a67ed4b010b0","description":"Bijan Robinson","sportId":28,"athleteId":4430807,"athlete":{"id":4430807,"description":"Bijan Robinson","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430807/bijan-robinson"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430807/bijan-robinson"}}}}},{"id":438528,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:20~l:28~a:4430878","guid":"edf87204-0e8c-331c-ac63-c6e04a89ee76","description":"Jaxon Smith-Njigba","sportId":28,"athleteId":4430878,"athlete":{"id":4430878,"description":"Jaxon Smith-Njigba","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430878/jaxon-smith-njigba"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430878/jaxon-smith-njigba"}}}}},{"id":529351,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:20~l:28~a:4426502","guid":"4eb7948a-431b-ee11-32de-2f4044548c60","description":"Drake London","sportId":28,"athleteId":4426502,"athlete":{"id":4426502,"description":"Drake London","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426502/drake-london"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426502/drake-london"}}}}},{"id":489617,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:20~l:28~a:4432665","guid":"bc4ba7ee-446b-36fd-9985-7fd2a94a98bc","description":"Brock Bowers","sportId":28,"athleteId":4432665,"athlete":{"id":4432665,"description":"Brock Bowers","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4432665/brock-bowers"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4432665/brock-bowers"}}}}},{"id":529915,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:20~l:28~a:4361741","guid":"d2e39a38-732d-5a24-f242-a4f9de87dabe","description":"Brock Purdy","sportId":28,"athleteId":4361741,"athlete":{"id":4361741,"description":"Brock Purdy","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361741/brock-purdy"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361741/brock-purdy"}}}}},{"id":167266,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:20~l:28~a:3040151","guid":"9c61fb91-fc5a-7cc3-8367-a8dbc589f97a","description":"George Kittle","sportId":28,"athleteId":3040151,"athlete":{"id":3040151,"description":"George Kittle","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3040151/george-kittle"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3040151/george-kittle"}}}}},{"id":9572,"type":"league","uid":"s:20~l:28","guid":"ad4c3bd2-ddb6-3f8c-8abf-744855a08fa4","description":"NFL","sportId":28,"leagueId":28,"league":{"id":28,"description":"NFL","abbreviation":"NFL","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/"}}}}}],"keywords":["Fantasy NFL","news - fantasy","news - fantasy football","Jahmyr Gibbs","Garrett Wilson","Geno Smith","Sam Darnold","Bijan Robinson","Jaxon Smith-Njigba","Drake London","Brock Bowers","Brock Purdy","George Kittle","NFL"],"story":"<p><photo1></p>\n<p>Everything that happens in the NFL has additional context when viewed from a <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/\">fantasy football</a> perspective. From position battles to injuries and so much more, the news cycle will constantly affect player values in fantasy football.</p>\n<p>Our fantasy football buzz file, with contributions from our ESPN fantasy writers and our NFL Nation reporters, aims to provide fantasy managers with the intel they need as news breaks around the league.</p>\n<h2>Sept. 27: Top fantasy scorers through Sunday Night Football</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><a data-player-guid=\"d85aed19-e3b8-3788-935e-55f636ad86e9\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4429795/jahmyr-gibbs\">Jahmyr Gibbs</a>, RB, <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"56caffee-178d-f6f2-a076-b277486b8c32\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/det/detroit-lions\">Detroit Lions</a> -- 41.4</li>\n<li><a data-player-guid=\"edf87204-0e8c-331c-ac63-c6e04a89ee76\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430878/jaxon-smith-njigba\">Jaxon Smith-Njigba</a>, WR, <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"3767a23c-a17d-294f-288a-9086ad1f0680\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/sea/seattle-seahawks\">Seattle Seahawks</a> -- 35.36</li>\n<li><a data-player-guid=\"6667bcb0-dad1-3345-8e5a-a67ed4b010b0\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430807/bijan-robinson\">Bijan Robinson</a>, RB, <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"49fd392a-86fe-4df3-1b77-9bbfa18b2ad5\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/atl/atlanta-falcons\">Atlanta Falcons</a> -- 35.3</li>\n<li><a data-player-guid=\"d2e39a38-732d-5a24-f242-a4f9de87dabe\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361741/brock-purdy\">Brock Purdy</a>, QB, <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"985a261f-296c-c95c-32a5-addc4df75001\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/sf/san-francisco-49ers\">San Francisco 49ers</a> -- 31.28</li>\n<li><a data-player-guid=\"4eb7948a-431b-ee11-32de-2f4044548c60\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426502/drake-london\">Drake London</a>, WR, Atlanta Falcons -- 28.4</li>\n<li><a data-player-guid=\"938f19a1-ef9b-618c-2365-d55291e0fcc6\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3912547/sam-darnold\">Sam Darnold</a>, QB, Seattle Seahawks -- 27.66</li>\n<li><a data-player-guid=\"bc4ba7ee-446b-36fd-9985-7fd2a94a98bc\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4432665/brock-bowers\">Brock Bowers</a>, TE, <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"b18540eb-6f2b-534c-e7f9-9bd930518da9\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/lv/las-vegas-raiders\">Las Vegas Raiders</a> -- 27.6</li>\n<li><a data-player-guid=\"da106063-995d-eaf0-54e4-ccecd5e90767\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4569618/garrett-wilson\">Garrett Wilson</a>, WR, <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"732d3caf-b350-1e34-48c6-b7cebb4a0d88\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/nyj/new-york-jets\">New York Jets</a> -- 26.7</li>\n<li><a data-player-guid=\"9c61fb91-fc5a-7cc3-8367-a8dbc589f97a\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3040151/george-kittle\">George Kittle</a>, TE, San Francisco 49ers -- 26.2</li>\n<li><a data-player-guid=\"593e3c58-2b92-e0f1-f4a8-84215e27f023\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/15864/geno-smith\">Geno Smith</a>, QB, New York Jets -- 26.04</li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>Click <a href=\"https://fantasy.espn.com/football/leaders?statSplit=singleScoringPeriod&scoringPeriodId=3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for a complete list of the week's leading fantasy scorers.</em></p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n\n<h2>Sept. 25: Bijan Robinson, Falcons offense back in a big way</h2>\n<p><photo2></p>\n<p><em>By Adam Rank</em></p>\n<p>Is <strong><a data-player-guid=\"28022fa1-9050-eee1-5160-c77a6a379ec2\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360423/michael-penix-jr\">Michael Penix Jr</a>.</strong> the MVP of the NFL? I mean, the dude might have a case right now after what the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"49fd392a-86fe-4df3-1b77-9bbfa18b2ad5\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/atl/atlanta-falcons\">Atlanta Falcons</a> did to the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"06cd3bcf-7a86-53d4-28e7-aa049dd36261\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/gb/green-bay-packers\">Green Bay Packers</a> on Thursday night. There hasn't been an upgrade this significant and this fast since Laney Boggs got rid of the glasses and paint-soaked smock in \"She's All That.\" But it's hard to ignore how good the Falcons looked on Thursday night. Let's take a look at some of the numbers from an incredible game. Well, incredible if you're both a fan of an NFC North team (like me) and also started<strong> <a data-player-guid=\"6667bcb0-dad1-3345-8e5a-a67ed4b010b0\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430807/bijan-robinson\">Bijan Robinson</a>.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Robinson had 213 scrimmage yards with a pair of touchdowns for 35.3 fantasy points.<strong> <a data-player-guid=\"4eb7948a-431b-ee11-32de-2f4044548c60\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426502/drake-london\">Drake London</a></strong> finished with just 194 receiving yards on 9 catches for 28.4 points. I mean, it seems paltry in comparison (it doesn't). Both guys were on fire. It was the third time they each had more than 150 in a single game. The Falcons were the first visiting team at Lambeau Field to produce a 150-yard rusher and receiver.</li>\n<li>For Robinson, it was his third game with 200 yards from scrimmage since 2023, tying <a data-player-guid=\"ddd8786c-fd5a-4e55-ccc8-6ddf6f1ede33\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4242335/jonathan-taylor\">Jonathan Taylor</a> for the most during that span. All three of these games have been in primetime.</li>\n<li>The Falcons found the red zone! The Falcons went 27 drives without reaching the red zone to start the season, but they made up for it after finally breaking the skid on the third drive of the game. But be honest, you were nervous when Penix opened the game with the interception? It's ok, we were all a little nervous.</li>\n<li>Some other good news is that London and <strong><a data-player-guid=\"7290d27f-bdc5-21fe-0800-c4ae5597cd34\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360248/kyle-pitts-sr\">Kyle Pitts Sr</a>.</strong> combined for 214 receiving yards! All right the four points from Pitts wasn't ideal. I do have more hope that he's going to break out of his season-opening skids. I mean, four points seem massive compared to where he was to start the season. But Penix makes this offense more dynamic and raises the bar for everyone.</li>\n<li>London has 100 receiving yards in six of his past seven games with Penix.</li>\n<li>The Packers were still able to put up big numbers for <strong><a data-player-guid=\"8f25b6b0-99c7-1923-dc47-13b3135ba608\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4248528/christian-watson\">Christian Watson</a></strong> and <strong><a data-player-guid=\"c5e38ead-375e-3df1-8989-1d7b334915a7\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4701936/matthew-golden\">Matthew Golden</a></strong>. Which is what we are really concerned about here, right? Watson became the first Packers receiver to open the season with a touchdown in three consecutive games since <a data-player-guid=\"d287bc03-47c2-c7f6-6160-e4280c80d2e2\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/16800/davante-adams\">Davante Adams</a> in 2018. Golden was targeted 12 times and turned that into 5 receptions for 100 yards and a touchdown.</li>\n<li>The Packers are putting up some fantasy numbers, which is great. But if this offense is truly going to get rolling again, it needs to run the football. The Packers rushed for 17 yards on Thursday night. That was the third-lowest total in club history since 1933.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b><a href=\"https://fantasy.espn.com/football/leaders\">Week 3 Scoring Leaders</a> >></b></p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n\n<h2>Sept. 24: Giants' Nabers (shoulder) trending in right direction for Sunday</h2>\n<p><photo3></p>\n<p><img class=\"floatleft\" src=\"https://a.espncdn.com/combiner/i?img=/i/teamlogos/nfl/500/nyg.png&w=110&h=110\" width=\"30\"> <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"378600ea-2397-8364-8399-b7c1606a49a7\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/nyg/new-york-giants\">New York Giants</a> wide receiver <a data-player-guid=\"44a2174b-1d11-3acf-8e75-fe0c13db47a6\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4595348/malik-nabers\">Malik Nabers</a> practiced for a second straight day Thursday and said he's feeling good and should be fine after injuring a shoulder Monday night against the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"2e1473b2-e269-fd7a-1137-c1edacb85986\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/lar/los-angeles-rams\">Los Angeles Rams</a>. Nabers looks like he's trending toward playing Sunday against the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"0a0aea59-9a5e-01b3-57a3-0151cf4bf393\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/ten/tennessee-titans\">Tennessee Titans</a> without any playing-time restrictions. An X-ray earlier in the week on Nabers' injured shoulder didn't reveal any serious problems. \"Good results,\" he said. \"I'm smiling. I'm out there playing, catching the ball. So, good results.\" -- <em>Jordan Raanan, NFL Nation</em></p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n\n<p><a name=\"buzztag\"></a></p>\n\n\n<h2>Sept. 23: Need a QB before Week 3? The best reliable, under-the-radar options</h2>\n<p><photo4></p>\n<p><em>By Tristan H. Cockcroft</em></p>\n<p>You couldn't find much more contrast between Weeks 1 and 2 of this NFL season.</p>\n<p>A week after the NFL matched the opening-week record for points scored (791), the 32 teams combined to score only 647 in Week 2. Per ESPN Research, the 647 are the fewest points in any non-Week 18 slate since Week 2 of the 2024 season.</p>\n<p>Injuries had quite a bit to do with it, particularly at the quarterback position. Through two weeks, we've already seen five starters depart games due to injury, and that excludes the <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/atl/atlanta-falcons\">Atlanta Falcons</a>' two combatants for their starting job (<a data-player-guid=\"3858bbe0-6348-e3ef-5d9f-2dd2acb46f44\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4241479/tua-tagovailoa\">Tua Tagovailoa</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"28022fa1-9050-eee1-5160-c77a6a379ec2\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360423/michael-penix-jr\">Michael Penix Jr</a>.) who have yet to play in 2026. Among the quarterbacks expected to be absent for Week 3 are three members of the position's top 10 in terms of ADP (average draft position): <a data-player-guid=\"f03f3238-b035-6f0e-5844-1529ca021c3a\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426348/jayden-daniels\">Jayden Daniels</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"13e97d3e-2171-371b-9a7a-2c44670b5a62\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4689114/jaxson-dart\">Jaxson Dart</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"dd15176c-3004-333f-beaa-149216c42968\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431611/caleb-williams\">Caleb Williams</a>.</p>\n<p>These high-profile injury setbacks have sent many a fantasy manager scrambling to find a quality quarterback, and there are plenty of options out there to be had -- standard, Knockout, Vampire, etc., leagues alike. Three in particular stand out, players who went 17th or later at the position in the preseason but are suddenly viable starters:</p>\n<p><b><a data-player-guid=\"0eb2837a-e6ed-bbd7-d7d5-cbeb2cd7ab11\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360689/tyler-shough\">Tyler Shough</a>, <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"97d2f6c9-2f22-459c-306a-046941ccab2a\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/no/new-orleans-saints\">New Orleans Saints</a>:</b> His <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/49954186/fantasy-football-rankings-consistency-ratings-start-sit-value\" target=\"_blank\">Consistency Ratings</a> won't reflect it due to his initial backup status to begin last season, but if we splice Shough's results into the games he started versus served in a backup capacity, he has been remarkably reliable. He's one of five quarterbacks to score 20-plus fantasy points in each of 2026's first two weeks, finishing eighth in scoring at the position in each, and he has been a top-10 scorer in five of his past seven starts.</p>\n<p>Shough still has inconsistencies, especially with how deliberate he has been with his throws early in those games (not to mention taking too many sacks), but the mettle he has shown while leading his team to an overtime loss and a win over the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"38248455-3da4-84e4-8090-98b5cc38ffdc\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/bal/baltimore-ravens\">Baltimore Ravens</a> speaks highly for his future potential. Shough is already in my top 10 rankings for Week 3 (LV) -- he was my must-get in our staff Vampire league -- and he has a good matchup for Week 4 (ATL), too.</p>\n<p>Shough, incidentally, leads all quarterbacks in <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/49869566/2026-fantasy-football-expected-fantasy-points-xfp-qb\" target=\"_blank\">expected fantasy points</a>, yet he's still out there in 32.1% of ESPN leagues.</p>\n<p><b><a data-player-guid=\"987f4f39-ed6f-5915-57eb-ec7dc356171c\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3046779/jared-goff\">Jared Goff</a>, <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"56caffee-178d-f6f2-a076-b277486b8c32\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/det/detroit-lions\">Detroit Lions</a>:</b> The one of these three who <i>wasn't</i> out there in any of our staff leagues, Goff was the QB17 in terms of ADP during the preseason, despite the high-octane offense he leads and the supremely favorable schedule his team faces in 2026. He's fourth on the aforementioned expected fantasy points list, and he turned in a top-10 weekly quarterback score in 42% of his games since the beginning of 2024. While unfortunately unavailable in any of our staff leagues, Goff was a clear QB2 target of mine in my home two-quarterback league, and he's still out there in 24.9% of ESPN leagues.</p>\n<p><b><a data-player-guid=\"975cc6da-01e5-3dcc-8a1a-1c9ecdb27d58\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4685720/bryce-young\">Bryce Young</a>, <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"647c27bf-ab86-550e-5b83-91c29e73e4a9\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/car/carolina-panthers\">Carolina Panthers</a>:</b> Admittedly, it's tough to rely on a quarterback who in only six of his 30 starts in 2024-25 combined earned a place in your fantasy lineup -- meaning a top-10 weekly positional score -- with five of those coming across the season's final eight weeks. But Young looks like a decidedly different player this year, particularly his improvements on deep throws. On attempts of 10 air yards or greater, he has completed 68% of his passes, more than 23% better than his career rate entering 2026 and been off-target on only 24%, down 11%. At the very least, Young is now a streaming option, and he has a good Week 3 matchup in the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"539babc5-e5fb-753b-8ae1-c15032a91ef4\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/cle/cleveland-browns\">Cleveland Browns</a>. He's also out there in 40.4% of ESPN leagues.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr>\n\n\n<h2>Sept. 23: RB Brooks out for at least six weeks</h2>\n\n\n<p><photo5></p>\n<p><strong><a data-player-guid=\"c349695b-9c76-39bf-878f-699e76ba2131\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4678008/jonathon-brooks\">Jonathon Brooks</a></strong> is set to miss <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50012387/sources-panthers-rb-jonathon-brooks-set-surgery-ir-move\">at least six weeks</a> after undergoing core muscle surgery, leaving <strong><a data-player-guid=\"7c6b0551-49b5-aa13-9e26-7db2f9dad46f\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4241416/chuba-hubbard\">Chuba Hubbard</a></strong> as the undisputed No. 1 in Carolina's backfield with <a data-player-guid=\"7d561919-7fde-fbee-8c41-eb0805faa25f\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4239934/aj-dillon\">AJ Dillon</a> as the backup.</p>\n<p>In this week's <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50012581/facts-vs-feelings-fantasy-advice-week-3\">Facts vs. Feelings</a>, Liz Loza pointed out that Hubbard finished as fantasy's RB10 in both Week 1 and Week 2, commanding Carolina's backfield with 27 touches for 151 scrimmage yards and three total touchdowns. </p>\n<p>She was already treating Hubbard as a low-tier RB 2 for his matchup against the Browns.</p>\n<p>NFL Nation's Mike Kaye reports that the Panthers will bring in <a data-player-guid=\"5a100261-ef63-1420-6cf7-539b6ac1725d\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3068267/austin-ekeler\">Austin Ekeler</a> for a workout. At this point it is too early to make a speculative add in anything but the deepest of formats.</p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n\n\n<h2>Sept. 22: Giants take a hit with loss of Jaxson Dart, uncertainty around Bears starting QB</h2>\n<p><photo6></p>\n<p><em>By Michael F. Florio</em></p>\n<p>Adam Schefter reported Tuesday that tests revealed that <a data-player-guid=\"13e97d3e-2171-371b-9a7a-2c44670b5a62\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4689114/jaxson-dart\">Jaxson Dart</a>'s knee injury is worse than initially thought, and the QB is now facing the <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50007211/sources-giants-qb-jaxson-dart-extended-period\">possibility of season-ending surgery</a>. Dart missing the season would be a crushing blow for the fantasy stock of Giants players.</p>\n<p><inline5></p>\n<p><a data-player-guid=\"57af2581-cec9-d5a3-2afe-7a719925f78b\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2969939/jameis-winston\">Jameis Winston</a> is the next man up. While that has meant good things for his receivers in the past, he looked rough Monday night. Given his past tendencies to lock in and pepper his top receiver with targets, <a data-player-guid=\"44a2174b-1d11-3acf-8e75-fe0c13db47a6\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4595348/malik-nabers\">Malik Nabers</a> still has fantasy hope. While this news drops Nabers into more of the WR2 range for the rest of the season, he still brings upside given his immense talent ... just expect more weekly volatility as well. If Nabers managers are panicking after his 1.1 fantasy points Monday with Winston under center, it could be a good time to buy low.</p>\n<p><a data-player-guid=\"b36df804-8242-754d-43b1-9dec06fafcaf\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361050/isaiah-likely\">Isaiah Likely</a> remains a TE1, though his fantasy ceiling does take a hit here (Likely was targeted nine times by Winston for a 33% target share). While this news could mean the Giants become a more run-heavy offense, that would help keep <a data-player-guid=\"0be760c4-3eb7-338a-9b0b-20de5895543c\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4696981/cam-skattebo\">Cam Skattebo</a> afloat. His fantasy value still takes a slight hit as there will be less consistent scoring chances without Dart, but he should see enough volume to remain in the low-end RB2 range.</p>\n<p>Some QBs managers can look to add to replace Dart in one-QB leagues are <a data-player-guid=\"9bef707d-d33f-266b-3020-81900d735915\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3917315/kyler-murray\">Kyler Murray</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"0eb2837a-e6ed-bbd7-d7d5-cbeb2cd7ab11\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360689/tyler-shough\">Tyler Shough</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"975cc6da-01e5-3dcc-8a1a-1c9ecdb27d58\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4685720/bryce-young\">Bryce Young</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"147e6862-2ac0-3a97-8f36-e3b1c0147320\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4432577/cj-stroud\">C.J. Stroud</a>. As for Winston, he is purely an option for superflex leagues and is more of a depth QB3 than a starter.</p>\n<p><strong>Bears' starting QB up in the air for Week 3</strong></p>\n<p><photo7></p>\n<p><a data-player-guid=\"4018c360-10de-36b9-b13b-847a6898c00e\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4434153/tyson-bagent\">Tyson Bagent</a> is in the concussion protocol, and his status is up in the air for Week 3. With <a data-player-guid=\"dd15176c-3004-333f-beaa-149216c42968\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431611/caleb-williams\">Caleb Williams</a> dealing with a hamstring injury, that would leave veteran <a data-player-guid=\"8d0f04b5-96e8-6985-13e2-0fa770882d9c\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/15168/case-keenum\">Case Keenum</a> as the starter for the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"19d73366-b5a5-cca2-a176-a2c024ce0bb3\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/chi/chicago-bears\">Chicago Bears</a>. To make matters trickier, the Bears play on \"Monday Night Football,\" so fantasy managers will have to decide what to do with their Bears players on Sunday, potentially without knowing who will be starting at QB.</p>\n<p>For those looking to replace Williams, the options to replace Dart (<a data-player-guid=\"9bef707d-d33f-266b-3020-81900d735915\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3917315/kyler-murray\">Murray</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"0eb2837a-e6ed-bbd7-d7d5-cbeb2cd7ab11\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360689/tyler-shough\">Shough</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"975cc6da-01e5-3dcc-8a1a-1c9ecdb27d58\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4685720/bryce-young\">Young</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"147e6862-2ac0-3a97-8f36-e3b1c0147320\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4432577/cj-stroud\">Stroud</a>) are good options here, too. For those in superflex, your options are more limited, as you can add <a data-player-guid=\"33be1f4a-d812-75b9-7b7c-5319d2a7113a\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2576980/marcus-mariota\">Marcus Mariota</a> or <a data-player-guid=\"57af2581-cec9-d5a3-2afe-7a719925f78b\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2969939/jameis-winston\">Winston</a>.</p>\n<p>The bigger fantasy question is what should fantasy managers do with their Bears in a tough matchup against the Eagles? <a data-player-guid=\"53a49a95-4f5b-fb94-9672-ef5787f431ee\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4259545/dandre-swift\">D'Andre Swift</a>, who has seen safe volume as a runner and receiver, is the Bear you can start with the most confidence. <a data-player-guid=\"b00b9764-fa7b-326a-ba35-9676bab28b09\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4608686/kyle-monangai\">Kyle Monangai</a> would be a flex option who could see a boost in volume, as the Bears likely would try to run more than usual. Last season against Philly, Swift ran for 125 yards and a touchdown, adding in a 13-yard catch. Monangai ran for 130 yards and a touchdown.</p>\n<p>The Bears' pass catchers have been disappointing to start the season, and in this matchup, with potentially a third-string QB, none are must-starts. <a data-player-guid=\"774cc71b-e83e-340d-bcda-4a8558265bb5\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431299/rome-odunze\">Rome Odunze</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"f78ad5c7-c991-3940-b213-79f9a8d77008\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4685278/luther-burden\">Luther Burden III</a> are both outside the top 30 WRs in ESPN consensus <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/page/FFWeeklyPlayerRank26main-49797082/fantasy-football-rankings-2026-qb-rb-wr-te-dst\">Week 3 rankings</a> and should be viewed as \"boom or bust\" flex options.</p>\n<p><a data-player-guid=\"678445c0-543b-31f1-b924-67545f33ebbb\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4723086/colston-loveland\">Colston Loveland</a> has been the biggest fantasy disappointment on the Bears to start the season. Through two games, he has just one catch for 3 yards (the third-most yards among Bears TEs). On top of that, the Eagles have allowed the second-fewest yards to tight ends this season, after allowing the second-fewest yards to the position in 2025. Some tight ends I would play over him are <a data-player-guid=\"d4652b30-6ba5-b261-e946-eb83b36a9b88\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4385690/dalton-kincaid\">Dalton Kincaid</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"9c61fb91-fc5a-7cc3-8367-a8dbc589f97a\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3040151/george-kittle\">George Kittle</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"b36df804-8242-754d-43b1-9dec06fafcaf\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361050/isaiah-likely\">Isaiah Likely</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"c7de446c-056d-5255-ba6e-47b061c83c98\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4572680/tucker-kraft\">Tucker Kraft</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"6713c2d0-5594-f7b2-a1bc-f2a53b907fc0\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3117256/dalton-schultz\">Dalton Schultz</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"897a7b37-1f13-3f52-b2ed-a45faef85eb1\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4570037/terrance-ferguson\">Terrance Ferguson</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Sept. 21: <a data-player-guid=\"9bef707d-d33f-266b-3020-81900d735915\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3917315/kyler-murray\">Kyler Murray</a> clears protocol, will start Week 3</h2>\n<p><photo8></p>\n<p><em>By Michael F. Florio</em></p>\n<p>Kyler Murray has cleared the concussion protocol and <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/49999840/vikings-murray-clears-concussion-protocol-start-vs-bucs\">will start in Week 3</a> against the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"13e8b157-a75a-ff24-ae91-fa3d52ddf204\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/tb/tampa-bay-buccaneers\">Tampa Bay Buccaneers</a>. We have not seen much of Murray in a Vikings uniform, but he brings QB1 upside due to his rushing ability and the matchup.</p>\n\n\n<p>The Bucs have allowed 234 passing yards per game, which ranks 11th highest in the NFL. That is after allowing the sixth-most passing yards in the NFL in 2025. Last week they allowed 19.72 fantasy points to <a data-player-guid=\"b6ec8e9e-3d85-a1de-9d0a-5a51621a9c20\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3122840/deshaun-watson\">Deshaun Watson</a>, 11th-best among QBs through Sunday.</p>\n\n\n<p>Murray was a fantasy target of mine this summer due to him being in the best system of his career, with great pass catchers around him. He has been top 12 in fantasy points per game among QBs in every year but one of his career. That is largely due to his rushing ability and highlights the safe floor he brings.</p>\n\n\n<p>Some QBs I would start him over in Week 3 are <a data-player-guid=\"2fbd2f9e-624d-3e63-9bb5-9bb965782b68\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431452/drake-maye\">Drake Maye</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"20c41c33-a33f-6dc2-7e1f-0771e39ce49a\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/12483/matthew-stafford\">Matthew Stafford</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"5bb4376a-d089-e3e4-e49a-44f1d709a012\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3052587/baker-mayfield\">Baker Mayfield</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"f19ea9a5-ca4d-79b9-3e49-543e438cd336\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4036378/jordan-love\">Jordan Love</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Which Commanders should you start with Daniels out?</h3>\n\n\n<p><a data-player-guid=\"33be1f4a-d812-75b9-7b7c-5319d2a7113a\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2576980/marcus-mariota\">Marcus Mariota</a> is expected to start Week 3 for the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"fbeaf73e-6d6c-cca4-0809-713d9d741f90\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/wsh/washington-commanders\">Washington Commanders</a> as <a data-player-guid=\"f03f3238-b035-6f0e-5844-1529ca021c3a\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426348/jayden-daniels\">Jayden Daniels</a> continues to seek opinions on his dislocated left elbow. Daniels does not have a timetable as of now.</p>\n\n\n<p>Mariota started eight games for the Commanders last season, averaging 200 passing yards and 32 rushing yards per game. He threw 10 touchdowns and added another with his legs.</p>\n\n\n<p>Mariota is not someone fantasy managers should be looking to force into their lineups. He is more an option for those in superflex leagues who now find themselves in a pinch. He brings a safer floor than you might expect, thanks to the rushing numbers, but falls far short of Daniels' ceiling.</p>\n\n\n<p>Washington faces the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"3767a23c-a17d-294f-288a-9086ad1f0680\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/sea/seattle-seahawks\">Seattle Seahawks</a> in Week 3, so even those in superflex leagues should look in another direction to help replace Daniels in their starting lineup. I would also recommend trying to avoid the Commanders' pass catchers in this one. <a data-player-guid=\"04454e17-9294-6271-f951-c0339528e97e\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3121422/terry-mclaurin\">Terry McLaurin</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"d6ba7023-458c-f59a-4af2-638770067518\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2976212/stefon-diggs\">Stefon Diggs</a> remain the team's top options, but they are more \"boom-or-bust\" WR3 or flex plays.</p>\n\n\n<p>Mariota did throw four times each to McLaurin and <a data-player-guid=\"2c787d57-fd60-9e8b-1e7f-d8aecc7a4cbb\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361577/dyami-brown\">Dyami Brown</a> in Week 2. He threw three times to Diggs, but the duo did connect for a touchdown.</p>\n\n\n<h3><a data-player-guid=\"de06715d-5216-76ee-f063-dabb342c4225\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3121023/dallas-goedert\">Dallas Goedert</a> to miss time</h3>\n\n\n<p>Goedert suffered a sprained MCL and is expected to miss a few weeks, per <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50000641/sources-eagles-te-dallas-goedert-mcl-sprain\">Adam Schefter and Ian Rapoport</a>. Goedert exited early in Week 2, playing only 26% of the snaps.</p>\n\n\n<p>Goedert was the go-to receiving option in the red zone for the Eagles, evident by his two Week 1 touchdowns. The Philadelphia tight ends room is very thin at the moment with rookie <a data-player-guid=\"7251cc73-0070-36d4-bf32-403bd63ad776\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4431574/eli-stowers\">Eli Stowers</a> on injured reserve. That likely leads to an uptick in targets for the Eagles' receivers. <a data-player-guid=\"323bc065-b098-29fc-a946-25c0c2752929\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4428850/dontayvion-wicks\">Dontayvion Wicks</a> should be added off waivers. <a data-player-guid=\"d7e2315a-4185-3bb5-846b-9e6acda6fa19\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4870795/makai-lemon\">Makai Lemon</a> remains an upside stash.</p>\n\n\n<p><a data-player-guid=\"6713c2d0-5594-f7b2-a1bc-f2a53b907fc0\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3117256/dalton-schultz\">Dalton Schultz</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"18c1eb5c-dfda-3e1c-ee18-2946bbbf6015\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3929645/juwan-johnson\">Juwan Johnson</a>, <a data-player-guid=\"d8843331-59d8-249e-7862-3b75104db19b\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2576925/darren-waller\">Darren Waller</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"55ebcec4-998f-316b-b228-319e079772d4\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4595342/oronde-gadsden\">Oronde Gadsden</a> are tight ends fantasy managers in need can look to add off the waiver wire.</p>\n\n\n\n\n","allowAMP":true,"allowAds":true,"allowComments":true,"allowCommerce":true,"allowContentReactions":true,"allowSearch":true,"byline":"ESPN Fantasy","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/40699880"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=40699880"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/wireless/story?storyId=40699880"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/40699880/fantasy-football-injuries-position-battles-nfl-news-analysis"}},"premium":false}],"breakingNews":[],"timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:57:22Z","status":"success"}